## Harness & CI Guidance
1. **Layered execution**: run traditional tests (`cargo test`, `bun test`, targeted scripts) before UI/E2E automation, then schedule nightly LLM smoke runs using orchestrator prompts derived from the tables above.
2. **LLM harness**: feed scenario metadata (trigger, preconditions, expected signals) into the orchestrator prompt so agent-based tests can self-verify and emit structured pass/fail JSON back to CI.
3. **Telemetry requirements**: expose structured logs/events for every “Signals” column; CI parsers can then assert outcomes without flaky visual checks.
4. **Fixture strategy**: provide mock AI providers, MCP servers, Safari stubs, and permission shims to keep runs deterministic.
